          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Why does low iron make people tired?",
          "answer": "Low iron levels can lead to tiredness because iron is essential for producing hemoglobin, the protein in red blood cells that carries oxygen throughout the body. When iron stores are low, the body produces smaller and paler red blood cells, which can result in reduced oxygen delivery to tissues. This lack of adequate oxygen can contribute to feelings of fatigue and weakness. This information comes from the document titled \"Iron-deficiency anemia.\"\n\nIf you have more specific questions on treatment options, lifestyle recommendations, or related topics, please feel free to ask!\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
